id: pm-mrhwow
title: Surface replication gate scopes trigger activation to relevant diff content
description: A declared trigger currently activates its full replication set for any change anywhere in the trigger file. The universal MCP output-budget schema legitimately changes tool-parameter-tables.ts but falsely activates the unrelated annotation-mutation-receipts set. Add declarative diff-content trigger predicates so the ratchet remains fail-closed for relevant contract changes without forcing unrelated churn.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-14T07:11:28.225Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-15T03:01:46.246Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-15T03:01:45.716Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-15T03:01:45.716Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Replication sets may declare content predicates for trigger-file diff hunks; Relevant annotation receipt changes still require every replicated member; Unrelated output-budget changes in the shared table do not activate annotation receipt replication; Negative-control tests prove malformed trigger declarations fail closed
parent: pm-92if
resolution: fixed
expected_result: "A replication set activates only when relevant contract lines change in a declared trigger file, still enforcing every required member and failing closed when diff evidence or trigger declarations are invalid."
actual_result: "The gate now supports changed_lines_contain_any markers, ignores proven unrelated hunks, activates on relevant added or removed lines, and treats unavailable diff evidence as active."
